      "encounter": { "reference": "Encounter/enc-3920" },
      "conclusion": "Minimally displaced fracture of the left proximal humerus (surgical neck). Diffuse osteopenia noted." } },
    { "resource": { "resourceType": "DocumentReference", "id": "doc-3922", "subject": { "reference": "Patient/CH-3390128" },
      "type": { "text": "Emergency department note" }, "date": "@D-150T09:10",
      "author": [{ "display": "Dr. Simone Achebe, MD" }],
      "context": { "encounter": [{ "reference": "Encounter/enc-3920" }], "practiceSetting": { "text": "Emergency Medicine" } },
      "content": [{ "attachment": { "contentType": "text/plain", "text": "Slipped on a wet bathroom floor, fell onto the left shoulder from standing height. X-ray: minimally displaced left proximal humerus fracture; radiologist notes diffuse osteopenia. Neurovascularly intact. Sling, analgesia, orthopedic follow-up in 1 week. Patient reports prior wrist, rib and foot injuries. No bone density study found in available records." } }] } },
