      "content": [{ "attachment": { "contentType": "text/plain", "text": "Acute left flank pain. CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast: 4 mm left distal ureteral stone with mild hydronephrosis. Serum calcium 11.2 mg/dL (H). Pain controlled; tamsulosin and strainer provided. Recommend primary care follow-up of elevated calcium and urology referral if stone does not pass." } }] } },
